Hide pathhide-matched files from /proc/<pid>/maps, smaps, smaps_rollup,
numa_maps and /proc/<pid>/fd (readdir, lookup, readlink and fdinfo).

Generated hunk by hunk against the real tree the fleet pins for this kernel
version:

    OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_common_oneplus_sm8550 @ oneplus/sm8550_b_16.0.0_oneplus_11

and dry-run at fuzz 0 against every distinct fs/proc variant the manifests
resolve to. A hunk that only lands "with fuzz" can silently guard the wrong
function, so treat a fuzz report from `patch` as a failure and regenerate.

Version notes:
  * proc_readfd_count()/proc_fd_getattr() do not exist here -- N/A, not skipped.
  * show_map()/show_smap() are wrapped rather than guarded inline: they open
    with get_pad_vma()/get_data_vma(), whose kzalloc'd copies are freed only by
    show_map_pad_vma(). An early return after those declarations would leak two
    struct vm_area_struct per hidden padded mapping, per read.
  * smaps_rollup iterates `for (vma = priv->mm->mmap; vma;)` with the advance at
    the bottom of the body, so the guard suppresses the accumulation rather than
    using `continue`, which would spin forever.
